@startuml fs_content_03_seq_revisions
skinparam backgroundColor #0F0E17
skinparam defaultFontColor #E5E7EB
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #A5B4FC
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #6366F1
skinparam sequenceGroupBackgroundColor #1A1830
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #6366F1
skinparam sequenceDividerBackgroundColor #1A1830
skinparam sequenceDividerFontColor #E5E7EB
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #1A1830
skinparam noteBorderColor #6366F1
skinparam noteFontColor #E5E7EB
skinparam titleFontColor #E5E7EB
skinparam ParticipantFontColor #E5E7EB
skinparam stateBackgroundColor #172554
skinparam stateBorderColor #6366F1
skinparam stateFontColor #E5E7EB
skinparam stateArrowColor #A5B4FC
title FS-CONTENT-03 (proposed) — Revision history and restore
autonumber "[00]"

actor "Owner" as O #1E1B4B
participant "Backoffice" as UI #172554
participant "Admin API" as API #172554
database "D1" as DB #052E16
participant "Edge cache" as C #052E16

== Every change writes a revision ==
O -> UI : Save, publish, unpublish or delete
UI -> API : request
API -> DB : BATCH: change the article AND insert a revision (kind, actor, body, sha256)
note over API, DB
  One transaction. A revision exists for every state the article was ever in.
  Older revisions beyond 50 per article and 180 days are pruned on write.
end note
API -> C : purge feed and article URLs

== Look back ==
O -> UI : History
UI -> API : GET /api/admin/articles/ID/revisions
API --> UI : list (time, who: admin or connector name, kind, size)
O -> UI : choose one
UI -> API : GET .../revisions/REV
API --> UI : text
UI --> O : the old text loaded into the editor as an unsaved change, with a diff

== Restore ==
O -> UI : Save the loaded text
UI -> API : PUT article
API -> DB : BATCH: update article, insert revision kind restore
note over API, DB
  Restoring never edits history: it adds a new revision on top.
  A restored published article reaches phones on their next sync.
end note

== Deleted articles ==
O -> UI : Recently deleted
UI -> API : GET /api/admin/articles/deleted
API --> UI : last deletes within 30 days
O -> UI : Restore as draft
API -> DB : BATCH: insert article from the last revision as a draft, insert revision
@enduml
